# MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Processing station
#
# Umbrella of this use case: the ontology header, which imports the module files under core/ and ext/.
# Single-file form: processing-merged.ttl (written by tools/merge_usecases.py).
#
# Notes carried over from the former plant.ttl, product.ttl, which this use case was split from;
# section titles and file names in them refer to those files.
#
# [plant.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - PROCESSING STATION - PLANT (DESIGN TIME)
#
# Sources (FESTO CD/03_Processing): 648813_Manual_Processing (DE/EN 04/06
# R2.2), Electric_Circuit_Diagram_Processing (drawing 195782, 05.04.06),
# 526882_Parts_list_Processing, assembly instructions (Processing,
# Drilling,
# Indexing table), data sheets, 03_Processing_GRAFCET (DE 01/04).
#
# The station uses only electrical actuators; the English commissioning
# text still lists a 6 bar air supply, the German text does not, so no
# compressed air is modelled. Motor ratings differ between the circuit
# diagram (M1 5 W, M2 5 W, M3 25 W) and the data sheets; both are kept
# in the descriptions.
#
# STATION
#
# Material number 526882 (parts list) and manual order number 648813.
#
# TECHNICAL DATA
#
# Static values from the manual's technical-data table and commissioning
# section.
#
# BILL OF MATERIALS
#
# Parts list 526882 (11.11.2002) with the components of the circuit
# diagram below each assembly.
#
# SIGNALS (DATA POINTS)
#
# Bits, XMA2 pins and BMKs from the electric circuit diagram, pages 4-7.
# Sensor = maestro:Output / maestro:DtdlTelemetry; actuator command = maestro:Input /
# maestro:DtdlProperty.
#
# I/O PATH: SYSLINK ENDPOINTS AND DATA INTERFACES
#
# XMA2 digital, XMG1 console. The URNs only name the connectors.
#
# [product.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS - PROCESSING STATION - PRODUCT (RECIPES)
#
# Source: the GRAFCET function chart of the Processing station
# (03_Processing_GRAFCET.pdf).
#
# The station's control sequence as an maestro:Recipe. Steps are realised by
# the skills of plant.ttl; data bindings connect parameters declared
# there. The workpiece itself and the line recipe are in
# line/product.ttl.
#
# CONTROL SEQUENCE (GRAFCET)
#
# One maestro:PlanStep per GRAFCET step with an action; maestro:stepOrder is the
# GRAFCET step number. Empty steps (1, 6, 10, 12, 13, the macro entry and
# exit steps) and the flag steps 5 and 14 are folded into transition
# expressions. Step 11 forks into the three parallel macro steps M20
# (drill hole checking, steps 21-23), M30 (drilling, 31-34) and M40
# (workpiece output, 41-42); each branch can skip to its exit step, which
# the Parallel constraints state. The bit shift of flag 'workpiece
# orientation' (step 14) is the data binding from the check to the
# drilling and output steps.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS - Processing station"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The Festo MPS Processing station of the LTU line: modules, parts list, I/O allocation and relay logic, skills, safety and care. The GRAFCET control sequence is an HHM-Core recipe in core/recipe.ttl. Built from manual 648813, the electric circuit diagram, parts list 526882, data sheets and the GRAFCET."@en ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/invocation>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/maas>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/policy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/product>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/recipe>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/resource>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/core/skill>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/automationml>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/dtdl>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/energy>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/isa95>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/maintenance>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/ext/runtime>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/shared> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .
